Group C of the [[2014 FIFA World Cup]] consisted of [[Colombia national football team|Colombia]], [[Greece national football team|Greece]], [[Ivory Coast national football team|Ivory Coast]], and [[Japan national football team|Japan]]. Play began on 14 June and ended on 24 June 2014. The top two teams, Colombia and Greece, advanced to the round of 16.

